    "field": "Climate model evaluation",
    "problem": "Attributing discrepancies between climate models and observations to either errors in simulated internal variability or the forced response is challenging because existing evaluation methods often rely on assumptions or filtering techniques to separate these intertwined signals.",
    "method": "We propose a methodological framework that uses large ensembles to evaluate how well climate models represent internal variability and forced response by assessing whether observations are distributed uniformly within the range of simulated climate states.",
    "task": "The task is to evaluate how well ten climate models represent internal variability and the response to external forcings in observed historical surface temperatures, using a methodological framework that exploits the power of large ensembles.",
